WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
[MUSIC INTRO]

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.650
OMAR RUTLEDGE: My
name is Omar Rutledge.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.200
When I was 19, I was
an infantry soldier

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.570
during the US invasion of Iraq.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.220
I found that returning
home was just

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.500
the beginning of my challenges.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.300
Everything seemed
totally different,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.430
even though it
all look the same.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.950
Somehow, the war changed me.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:20.970
But how?

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.200
And why?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.030
When I got out of
the Army, I wanted

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.920
to understand how experiencing
trauma changes the brain

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.790
and, more importantly, to try
to develop better treatments

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.259
to help people get
back to normal.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:35.400
This inspired me to
become a neuroscientist.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.710
As a graduate
student at MIT, I'm

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.360
learning how to
investigate the brain

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.240
through magnetic
resonance imaging or MRI.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.670
I am designing a clinical
trial to investigate

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.110
if the alternative medicine CBD
has an effect on social anxiety

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:54.130
disorder, the most common
anxiety disorder in the US.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:57.280
My hope is this research will
allow us to better understand

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.170
the effects of this
drug and how it

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:02.440
may be useful for the treatment
of mental health conditions.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.890
[MUSIC OUTRO]

